From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RootBeer <rootb33rman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:33:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Extended View Distance fixes

Failed and ungenerated reads stay cached for a few seconds instead of being read again every tick, where they also held back every farther fake chunk; cache entries expire a few seconds after a player last asked for them rather than living as long as any client holds the chunk, which kept every fake chunk ever sent in memory and every built but unsent one forever, and a watch racing the drain left an entry without a future that threw on the region thread. A real chunk leaving the load range is kept on the client as a fake chunk instead of being forgotten and rebuilt from disk, which sent it twice and left a hole where the chunk was not saved yet. Real and fake chunks share the send allocation, the visual distance stops at the client's view distance like the send distance does, and a player set to 0 gets no fake chunks. Light is sent as the live light engine sends it, so sections it leaves to the client are no longer sent dark, and chunks without valid light are lit by the sky instead of sent black. Chunks saved by a newer version are skipped instead of stopping the server, and hidden ores keep the stone they sit in.

